These fixes justify checking exact commits/backports and capabilities. They
do not justify promoting DMA based solely on a >=7.2 version check. ublk batch
and descriptor tuning should follow correctness and measured bottlenecks.
The ordinary shared-tag design aims to remove one explicit CPU memcpy while
retaining the traditional ublk copy; platform DMA bounce copies are outside
that count and must be checked on the target device.
